//! Change, Git, and preflight tools.

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const GET_DEPENDENTS: &str = "Bounded transitive reverse blast radius: who depends on this symbol. Pass label for one symbol, or path for the declarations in that file. With both, an ambiguous label is the declaration that lives in that file. repository reads a child directory of the launch root and does not move the process pin. The seed and each dependent are id, label, kind, language, and span. depth and max_nodes bound the walk. precision, max_references, timeout_ms, and include_container_importers further bound it. A missing label is an error. An ambiguous label without a distinguishing path is an error that lists ids.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const CHANGE_IMPACT: &str = "Read-only blast radius. files, or the deprecated target alias, names the files. A named file with no measured diff seeds its symbols as change file_scope: a hypothetical scope, and not a git edit. base, base_ref, head_ref, or diff selects a measured change instead. status stays COMPLETE when the tool ran. Read evidence_completeness and stop_reason. stop_reason MAX_NODES means the combined cap omitted nodes. max_nodes defaults to 40 and keeps production callers ahead of tests. depth bounds the walk. Impacted nodes are id, label, kind, language, and span. Measured coverage is not read. ci_protection is not included. precision, max_references, and timeout_ms further bound the walk.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const SELECT_TESTS: &str = "Select the test files a change most plausibly needs to run. Pass files, the deprecated target alias, or a git range through base, base_ref, head_ref, or diff. Ranking is static: a changed test file, name overlap, dependents within depth (default 3, maximum 6), and a parent-directory mention when that directory name is at least 5 characters and is not a generic name such as src or tests. An empty tests array means no static match. It does not mean the repository has no tests. coverage_evidence.present stays false, and the reason says no measured per-test coverage was consumed. max_tests caps the list (default 100, maximum 500). max_nodes caps the dependent walk (default 200). This tool does not run tests.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const VERIFIED_CHANGE: &str = "Composite pre-commit evidence and a conservative verdict. task is required and is stored on the report. phase is plan (the default) or verify. Plan embeds at most 4 edit contexts; editContextsTotal and editContextsTruncated say when more existed. Each edit context keeps at most 8 relationship rows. On plan, audit, duplicates, architecture, and the graph baseline stay PLANNED. impact_depth is the blast-radius depth and max_impact_nodes is its max_nodes. Selected symbols are compact nodes. Data-flow edges are source, target, kind, and, when present, coupling and the call line, without provenance. data_flow_depth and max_data_flow_edges bound that flow (the plan default keeps the edge cap small). verdict PASS can still show changed_files length 0 when the scope is hypothetical. phase verify runs the audit, duplicate ratchet, and architecture check. duplicate_ratchet, api_contract, tests, run_tests, and test_timeout_ms choose those sections. source_mutation is NONE. The tool does not write source.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const PREPARE_CHANGE: &str = "Select the architecture rules that name an intended edit. files is a required array of repository paths. intent is an optional note and is echoed, not executed. Each file comes back with its contract component and the rules that apply to it. No contract yields state NOT_CONFIGURED, a starter contract, and write NONE. This does not verify the graph and does not write .weavatrix/architecture.json. Call verify_architecture for the verdict and explain_architecture_violation with a fingerprint from that verdict.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const GRAPH_DIFF: &str = "Compare the current snapshot with an immutable Git revision. base_ref is required. head_ref defaults to the worktree when omitted. detail file_pairs (the default) aggregates edge churn by source file, target file, and relation. detail edges returns individual edge provenance and is the larger answer. path limits the diff to one path. max_results pages the pairs or edges. token_budget trims the tail. ci_protection is not included. This reads git objects and does not check out a worktree.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const GIT_HISTORY: &str = "Bounded Git history read from the object store. The git executable is not launched. Pass path for commits that touch that file or directory; omit path for repository HEAD history. history_truncated true means a parent commit is missing, which is the shallow-clone boundary. It does not mean the start commit itself is missing: a missing start object is still an error. Hitting max_commits leaves history_truncated false on a repository-wide walk. A file history also treats the scan cap as truncation. months limits repository history. revision chooses the start commit. include_analytics adds hotspots and co-change and diffs every selected commit; omit it for the commit list. first_parent, min_pair_count, max_pairs, and top_n apply to analytics. token_budget trims commits from the tail. status COMPLETE means the walk answered.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const GIT_READ_BLOB: &str = "Bounded UTF-8 file content at an immutable Git revision or blob oid, without a checkout. Pass path plus revision (default HEAD), or oid for a blob object. A non-blob object is an error. A binary blob is an error: the tool serves text evidence only. max_bytes defaults to 262144 and must be from 1 to 2000000. truncated true means the byte cap cut the text on a character boundary. lines is the returned text split on newlines. token_budget can trim lines. The worktree file is left untouched. Use read_source for the current worktree.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const CROSS_REPO_GIT: &str = "Parallel histories, shared commits, or diffs across named local repositories. repositories is required. Each entry is a path string or an object with path. action selects the comparison. revision, base_ref, head_ref, left, right, max_commits, and first_parent bound it. The launch root stays pinned. This reads local git data and does not fetch. Call git_fetch first when the other repository is only a remote URL. An entry must be a path string or an object with path; an empty list is an error.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const GIT_FETCH: &str = "Shallow-clone one Git URL at one ref into a local cache and return that checkout. url is required: https, http, ssh, git, or file URL, scp-style git@host:path, or an absolute local path. A URL that embeds credentials is refused. A trailing .git names the same cache entry. ref is a branch, tag, or commit; omit it to fetch the remote HEAD. Depth is always 1. This launches git and writes only the cache. The process root stays pinned, and open_repo is still refused without --allow-retarget. The cache is not a substitute for the repository you already have open. git_history still reads the active repository.";
